# Files in this repository that must NOT be published as part of the site.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Everything in this folder is the deploy's asset
# directory, so by default every file here is fetchable at
# savesavesavesave.xyz/<filename>. That was confirmed, not assumed:
# https://savesavesavesave.xyz/README.md returned the whitepaper text in
# full. Nobody had chosen to publish it; it was simply in the folder.
#
# Format is the same as .gitignore. Wrangler skips matching files when it
# uploads assets, so they stay in version control and stop being URLs.
#
# WHAT STAYS PUBLIC, deliberately: the eleven HTML pages, paper.css, the
# images, favicon, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, ads.txt, LICENSE.md, and
# SaveSaveSaveSave-Whitepaper.pdf (linked from the site as a download).
#
# BEFORE ADDING A LINE HERE, check nothing on the site links to it. The
# only file the pages reference from this category is the PDF above, and
# it is deliberately not listed.


# ---- Internal documents ----------------------------------------------
# Written for the people building this, not for readers. The site is
# deliberately open about its limits — that is what Technical
# Transparency is for, curated and written to be read. A raw internal
# state file is a different thing, and the business proposal is not
# public material at all.
PROJECT-STATE.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
PAGES-SETUP.md
UPLOAD-NOTES.md
SaveSaveSaveSave_Wallet_Risk_Intelligence_Proposal.md

# Superseded whitepaper editions. Unlinked, but publicly fetchable and
# now CONTRADICTING the published HTML — a visitor who found one would
# be reading claims the site has since corrected. That is worse than a
# missing document.
SaveSaveSaveSave_Whitepaper_v3.0.md
SaveSaveSaveSave_Whitepaper_Short_v3.0.md

# Duplicates the whitepaper as raw markdown. Two copies of the same text
# at two URLs is a duplicate-content problem, and the HTML version is
# the one meant to be read.
README.md


# ---- Engine source ----------------------------------------------------
# These are embedded verbatim inside index.html, which is why the
# scanner works as a single self-contained file. Nothing fetches them,
# so serving them only publishes a second copy that can fall out of step
# with the page. The repository remains public; this is about which
# copy is authoritative.
core.js
scanmodel.js
promptscan.js
goplus-proxy-worker.js


# ---- Build and test tooling -------------------------------------------
# Developer tools. No visitor has a reason to fetch them.
*.test.js
redteam.js
apply-ads.js
embed.js
verify_embedded.js
build-sitemap.js
build-suffixes.js
make-pdf.js
shot.js
icons.py
switch-domain.sh
